## Environment Variables
See `.env.example`. Key ones:
- `DATABASE_URL` — PostgreSQL connection ({% if deploy_target == 'render' %}`render.yaml` sets it from the `{{ app_name }}-db` database{% else %}create-app sets it on the Railway service as a reference to the Postgres service{% endif %})
{% if auth_provider == 'google' %}- `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID` / `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET` — this app's own Google OAuth client
- `SESSION_SECRET` — signs the session cookie (at least 32 characters)
- `AUTH_ALLOWED_EMAILS` — who may sign in; empty means nobody
- `APP_BASE_URL` — public origin; on Render it defaults to `RENDER_EXTERNAL_URL`
- `AGENT_CREDENTIALS` — JSON list of agent key hashes
- The Google and agent key settings load only from this app's `.env` and the process environment, never from `~/.agentic-apps.env`
{% else %}- `LOGTO_ENDPOINT` / `LOGTO_APP_ID` / `LOGTO_APP_SECRET` — Auth credentials
- `LOGTO_API_RESOURCE` — API resource identifier for token audience
{% endif %}- `CORS_ORIGINS` — Comma-separated allowed origins{% if deploy_target == 'render' %}. Leave it unset on Render: the app then allows only `RENDER_EXTERNAL_URL`{% endif %}
{% if include_frontend and auth_provider == 'logto' %}- `VITE_LOGTO_APP_ID` / `VITE_LOGTO_ENDPOINT` / `VITE_LOGTO_API_RESOURCE` — Frontend auth (in `frontend/.env`)
{% endif %}
